1ec46900f2","file":"preprints/The-Strong-Hyperkahler-SYZ-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":25,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2a318829bdde5bce5da4ec00ad1ca2080adfdb66f9b52b50b9699162c8ef45b4","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Strong-Hyperkahler-SYZ-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5a03ae8fc82170cd12cc9cf6278b2fb58ef6948adc691f3f7784231ec46900f2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Strong-Hyperkahler-SYZ-Conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L25"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $X$ be a compact irreducible holomorphic symplectic K\\\"ahler\nmanifold of complex dimension $2n$, where $n\\ge1$. If a holomorphic\nline bundle $L$ satisfies\n\\[\n c_1(L)\\ne0,\\qquad c_1(L)\\in\\overline{\\mathcal K_X},\n                  \\qquad q_X(c_1(L))=0,\n\\]\nthen $L$ is semiample.\n\nMore precisely, there exist a positive integer $m$, a normal\nprojective variety $B$, an ample line bundle $A$ on $B$, and a\nsurjective holomorphic map with connected fibers\n\\[\n                 f:X\\longrightarrow B,\\qquad L^m\\simeq f^*A,\n\\]\nsuch that $\\dim_{\\C}B=n$. Every irreducible component of every\nfiber has complex dimension $n$, and $\\sigma$ vanishes on its\nsmooth locus."}
